Verification of L0/L1 on genuine Jacobian pairs (automorphisms of C^2):
  F=(x, y+x^3)
     deg=(1,3)  g=1  (a,b)=(1,3)  Jac=1
     L0: Jac(P_n,Q_m) = 0   OK
     L1: Jac(P_n,Q_{m-1})+Jac(P_{n-1},Q_m) = 0   OK
     P_n factors: x
     Q_m factors: x**3
  F=(x+y^2, y+(x+y^2)^3)
     deg=(2,6)  g=2  (a,b)=(1,3)  Jac=1
     L0: Jac(P_n,Q_m) = 0   OK
     L1: Jac(P_n,Q_{m-1})+Jac(P_{n-1},Q_m) = 0   OK
     P_n factors: y**2
     Q_m factors: y**6
  deeper composite
     deg=(12,6)  g=6  (a,b)=(2,1)  Jac=1
     L0: Jac(P_n,Q_m) = 0   OK
     L1: Jac(P_n,Q_{m-1})+Jac(P_{n-1},Q_m) = 0   OK
     P_n factors: y**12
     Q_m factors: y**6

ALL L0/L1 CHECKS PASS

Jung-van der Kulk consequence (degrees of automorphisms):
  every pair above has n|m or m|n -> (a,b) has a=1 or b=1, tower
  terminates immediately.  A counterexample needs a,b>=2 coprime,
  i.e. a NON-TRIVIAL continued fraction: this is the search lattice.
